#
# 8cu -- UPSTREAM 9front's 8c, linked against APExp's shared cc/.
#
# This is not a compiler anyone should use.  It is ONE EXPERIMENT,
# built the same way as every other backend here so that nothing about
# the build is a variable: see README in this directory.
#
# Deliberately NOT in sys/src/cmd/mkfile's DIRS.  One failing entry
# aborts the whole tree's mk, and a vendored copy that has never been
# compiled on this machine is exactly the kind of thing that would.
# Build it by hand:
#
#	cd sys/src/cmd/8cu && mk install
#
# TARG=8cu so it lands beside 8c in $objtype/bin rather than over it;
# mkfile.port sets BIN=$APEXPROOT/$objtype/bin (no /ape).
#
# OFILES is upstream's list MINUS 8c_vla.$O, which is APExp's own file
# and does not exist here.  Nothing in cc/ calls the one function it
# defines (gvlalloc), and gvla_prologue/gvla_epilogue have weak
# defaults in cc/vla.c, so dropping it costs nothing but VLA support --
# which this experiment does not use.
#
# T=8 makes mkfile.port's `enam.c: ../$D/$T.out.h' rule read
# ../8c/8.out.h.  That is APExp's copy and it is byte-identical to the
# one beside this file, so the generated enam.c is the same either way.
#
</$objtype/mkfile
APEXPROOT=../../../..
TARG=8cu
OFILES=\
	cgen.$O\
	cgen64.$O\
	div.$O\
	enam.$O\
	list.$O\
	machcap.$O\
	mul.$O\
	peep.$O\
	pgen.$O\
	pswt.$O\
	reg.$O\
	sgen.$O\
	swt.$O\
	txt.$O\

HFILES=\
	gc.h\
	8.out.h\
	../cc/compat.h\
	../cc/cc.h\

T=8
<../cc/mkfile.port
<$APEXPROOT/sys/src/cmd/mkone
